# Path-based ownership.
#
# There is one maintainer, so nothing here changes who gets asked. It is written down anyway
# because it is the only machine-readable statement of where the boundaries in this repository
# are - and because the day a second person arrives, the boundaries should already exist rather
# than be invented under time pressure.

# Default: everything goes to the owners.
*                                   @Jersyfi

# Areas where a change is particularly expensive to correct.
/docs/adr/                          @Jersyfi
/api/openapi.yaml                   @Jersyfi
/db/migrations/                     @Jersyfi
/.github/workflows/                 @Jersyfi
/core/domain/                       @Jersyfi
/LICENSE                            @Jersyfi
/CLAUDE.md                          @Jersyfi

# The clients and what they share (ADR-0027). Separate entries rather than one `/apps/` line:
# the two applications are unrelated to each other, and the design system governs both.
/apps/webapp/                       @Jersyfi
/apps/website/                      @Jersyfi
/packages/design-system/            @Jersyfi
/packages/api-client/               @Jersyfi

# The single source for every colour, spacing and duration in the product (ADR-0029). A change
# here changes what every client renders.
/packages/design-system/tokens/     @Jersyfi

# Generated into the core from the design system, and committed. A hand edit here is the drift
# the generator exists to prevent - CI catches it, and this makes it visible in review too.
/core/domain/model/shared/LabelTokens.go   @Jersyfi

# The interface adapter and the placeholder that keeps `go build` working without Node.js.
/presentation/webui/                @Jersyfi

# The container build now has a frontend stage; the promise it keeps is two containers.
/deploy/docker/                     @Jersyfi
